{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792262746,"nonce":"2xoSN1TX2iaBNiX8cH70t5mf93Q=","message":"Context: this is the uniform-entry gate, not an oversight. A signature wider than eight arguments is called through a 'uniform entry' the backend emits (one word per argument, re-applied with the real ABI). The LLVM tier does not emit one because widening that gate crashed MBHaxe at launch (d835154 put the default back to 8), so entry.uniform_addr is 0 and call_compiled_entry refuses. The Cranelift tier, hybrid and the interpreter run the same call correctly (TestDynCallManyArgs). Fixing this means proving the uniform entry on the LLVM tier first; priority stays low.","files":null}]}